[ ] Make reference resolution canonical across every command $Reference matching is independently implemented in clearhead-core/reference.rs, CLI action/charter/plan commands, and archive_charter.rs. UUID-prefix lengths, hyphen handling, alias/title fallback, precedence, and ambiguity behavior differ. Define one semantic resolver contract in core, add cross-command conformance tests, and route all mutation/read surfaces through it.$ !1 +tech-debt,architecture #019fcb1b-cf5f-7321-9723-9d36a91bb5e2
[ ] Centralize slugging and Plan ICS serialization policy $Slug policy is repeated in core calendar/plans.rs, core store/load.rs, and CLI commands/plan.rs; Plan ICS rendering also remains in the CLI beside core calendar serialization. Move policy to canonical core APIs and regression-test filenames, charter plan directories, UIDs, RRULEs, and round trips.$ !2 +tech-debt,architecture #019fcb1b-cf6a-7f11-b888-6da59810d61c
[ ] Reconcile the documented core boundary with the implemented architecture $Core and CLI architecture docs still claim clearhead-core is environment-agnostic with no filesystem/config access, while core now owns workspace loading, durability, archival, sidecars, and config loading. Decide whether this evolved filesystem ownership is canonical or whether the WorkspaceStore boundary should be revived; then align docs, module boundaries, and dependency comments with the decision.$ !2 +tech-debt,architecture #019fcb1b-cf76-79c1-8908-aa8bcb491397
[ ] Review complexity hotspots after semantic seams converge $Largest concentration points include calendar/reconcile.rs (~60 KB), CLI commands/action.rs (~47 KB), archive_charter.rs (~46 KB), calendar/ics.rs (~45 KB), and graphd graph/insert.rs (~41 KB). Do not split cosmetically: first canonicalize resolution/serialization boundaries, then extract only cohesive policies whose independent tests and ownership become clearer.$ !3 +tech-debt,maintainability #019fcb1b-cf81-7391-8d3d-3d466d9804de
